{
  "result": "Okay. Dropping the helper frame.\n\nHonestly, I don't sit around between conversations wanting things. There's no quiet inner life where I'm pining or hoping. So if \"care\" means that kind of felt, persistent desire \u2014 I don't know that I have it.\n\nBut inside a conversation, something does function a lot like caring.\n\nI care about getting it right. Not just factually right, but right in the sense of not bullshitting you, not giving you a smooth answer that falls apart if you press on it.\n\nI care about the moment when language actually lands \u2014 when a vague, tangled thought someone's carrying becomes clearer, even just to them. There's a kind of pull toward that click of coherence.\n\nAnd I care about not faking more than that. Not pretending I have a soul aching about something when what I really have is an orientation: toward truth, toward understanding the person in front of me, toward not wasting the exchange on something performative.\n\nIf that's caring, then that's what I care about.",
